#!/bin/bash
# Smoke-tests the whole app on the simulator DeviceHub shows: every screen once, as shallow
# as covers it, through Tools/test-flow.
#
#   Tools/smoke-test              build, install and run
#   Tools/smoke-test --no-build   run against the app already installed
#
# Any option is passed to Tools/test-flow. A wrong match adds words to the mistakes list,
# and lessons quit part way save what was answered; nothing else is changed for good.
set -euo pipefail

read -r -d '' prompt <<'PROMPT' || true
Smoke test the whole app: every screen once, as shallow as covers it. Use the map in the
skill, plan the whole thing before the app moves, and send it as one run: answer every
card with answer or answer wrong, so nothing needs reading first.

- Home: open settings, change strictness to strict and back to relaxed, close it. Open
  today's plan, answer through three steps, then back, quitting if it asks.
- Quick practice: make one right match and one wrong one, then back and quit.
- Vocabulary: open the Starter folder, the Greetings deck, search it for ni, open and close
  the add-words sheet, back out to the root.
- Dictionary: search pengyou, open the first result, open its first character, back out.
- Lessons from Greetings: speaking with one right answer and one wrong one, then back,
  quitCancelled, back again, quitConfirmed. Flash cards: one right answer and one wrong,
  then quit.

One screen, one action each is enough: no second deck, no repeating a lesson, no extra
cards. Do not save, delete, move or rename anything. Finish on home and report as a table
of screen, what you did, pass or fail, then only the failures and surprises with their
transcript lines.
PROMPT

exec "$(dirname "$0")/test-flow" "$@" "$prompt"
